# A branch that has never been pushed. This is the commonest state in which a
# body is first written, so the verdict has to be neither an error nor a silent
# pass. The ref is DERIVABLE -- `origin/<branch>` -- it simply does not exist
# yet, and nothing is at risk: the push creates it, and the body reaches the
# pull request with `--body-file` at creation time, which is after it.
#
# BEFORE THE #694 REVIEW THIS SHAPE DID NOT REACH THIS ARM AT ALL. A branch cut
# with `git checkout -b foo origin/main` has an upstream from the moment it
# exists -- `origin/main` -- so a check reading `@{u}` compared a
# never-pushed branch against main rather than reporting that it could not
# compare. Deriving the ref from the branch's own name is what puts it here.
#
# <branch or -> <remote or -> <own-remote-ref sha or -> <behind> <ahead> <rc> <compared ref or -> <text>
never-pushed origin - 0 0 3 origin/never-pushed a branch with no remote branch yet reports that it cannot compare
